      "id": 1,
      "text": "Grassy Creek was founded around 1788 and quickly grew into one of Ashe County’s most prosperous agricultural communities by the early 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://alchetron.com/Grassy-Creek%2C-Ashe-County%2C-North-Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Greer family, raising purebred shorthorn cattle, established six farms that still define Grassy Creek’s landscape after four generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://theoldstoregrassycreek.com/pages/grassy-creek-north-carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A cheese factory opened in 1915, producing $1,500 worth of cheese in its first year before closing by 1920.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://theoldstoregrassycreek.com/pages/grassy-creek-north-carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Old Store, once a post office, doctor’s office, and general store, remains a community gathering spot rooted in Grassy Creek’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://theoldstoregrassycreek.com/pages/grassy-creek-north-carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1976 Grassy Creek became the first rural historic district listed on the National Register of Historic Places, a move that helped shield it from a proposed dam.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://theoldstoregrassycreek.com/pages/grassy-creek-north-carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The historic district contains 29 buildings and structures, many of which still stand today, echoing the town’s once-thriving community.",
